  "name": "Question 7",
  "problem": "Find the greatest common divisor of $6\\,624$ and $1\\,265.$",
  "worked_solution": "We use the Euclidean algorithm, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}6\\,624 & = & 1\\,265(5) & + & 299 \\\\  & ↙ &  & ↙ &  \\\\ 1\\,265 & = & 299(4) & + & 69 \\\\  & ↙ &  & ↙ &  \\\\ 299 & = & 69(4) & + & 23 \\\\  & ↙ &  & ↙ &  \\\\ 69 & = & 23(3) & + & 0\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe last positive remainder is $23.$ Therefore, we conclude that the greatest common divisor of $6\\,624$ and $1\\,265$ is $23.$ Symbolically, we write\n\n$$\n\\text{gcd}(6\\,624,1\\,265)=23.\n$$",
